The ability to identify gems only saves time. You can tell if a gem is 
valuable or not just by dropping it in a general store or jewellers shop.
Once you know that a gem is valuble you can name all gems of that class
as valuable using the #name command so that you will recognise that type
of gem in the future. Also name worthless gems so you will recoginse these.
I also do the same for lamps, if a lamp is normal I name the class 'normal',
this way I can recoginse a magic lamp easily because it won't be named.

 
